 Remainder Theorem, we need to evaluate \\(f(-5)\\) and set it equal to 4.\n\nFirst, substitute \\(x = -5\\) into the polynomial:\n\\[ f(-5) = k(-5)^4 + 9(-5)^3 + k(-5)^2 + 32(-5) - 11 \\]\n\nCalculate each term step by step:\n\\[ (-5)^4 = 625, \\quad (-5)^3 = -125, \\quad (-5)^2 = 25 \\]\n\nThus, the expression becomes:\n\\[ f(-5) = k(625) + 9(-125) + k(25) + 32(-5) - 11 \\]\n\\[ f(-5) = 625k - 1125 + 25k - 160 - 11 \\]\n\\[ f(-5) = 650k - 1296 \\]\n\nWe know that \\(f(-5) = 4\\), so we set up the equation:\n\\[ 650k - 1296 = 4 \\]\n\nSolve for \\(k\\):\n\\[ 650k = 4 + 1296 \\]\n\\[ 650k = 1300 \\]\n\\[ k = \\frac{1300}{650} \\]\n\\[ k = 2 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(k\\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{2}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
